&lt;p&gt;What are KYC-verified Binance accounts?&lt;br&gt;
KYC (Know Your Customer) verification on Binance refers to the process where customers are required to provide certain personal details and documents to prove their identity. The process is to ensure compliance with standard rules for cryptocurrency exchanges as well as banks that prevent money laundering, fraud, and other criminal acts.&lt;br&gt;
KYC verification for Binance typically requires the provision of various documents such as government-issued ID (e.g., passport, driver’s license) as well as proof of address (e.g., utility bills and bank statements). Sometimes, they will require additional details based on the degree of verification required.&lt;br&gt;
If an individual’s identity is confirmed, the account they have on Binance will be recognized as KYC confirmed. The KYC verification process often provides customers with additional benefits, including higher withdrawal limits, more advanced trading options, and more. It is important to note that KYC verification is a common process for many trusted exchanges like Binance, which helps ensure the safety and reliability of all users on the platform.&lt;br&gt;
